arch results, I found information about Arknights: Endfield's facility port placement system. While the search results discuss port mechanics and conveyor belt connections, I could not find the specific rules you mentioned about port placement on \"opposite sides\" or \"long side\" port direction.\n\nThe search results show that every machine has input and output slots, and conveyor belts move items between them. Additionally, if you connect a belt to the wrong side, the visuals may still look \"connected,\" but the objective won't advance because the game is validating the port.\n\nHowever, the specific facility port placement rules regarding \"opposite sides\" or \"long side\" port direction that you're asking about don't appear in these search results. The results focus more on general conveyor belt mechanics and connection procedures rather than specific placement rules for facility ports.\n\nIf you're looking for detailed information about these specific port placement rules in Endfield, you might want to check the official game documentation, wiki pages dedicated to factory mechanics, or community guides that specifically cover facility placement layouts.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b0b3ac5f-861c-4a73-a398-ae936a5ca7c9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:27.960Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"072d586d-47d6-41ba-a123-f7791a6b90c6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
